## build/yin-repl-peer

It needs a rebuild. The Dart peer compiles `yin.repl` through `main`, `driver` and `serve`, so it keeps the old rendering until `bb build:yin-repl-peer` runs. `bb test:cljd` already depends on that build.

## Open points

- `(prn +)` inside a program prints the nameless `{:type :host-fn}`. Those primitives are built before the VM exists and can't see its tables. Fixing it means passing the VM's tables into `make-repl-primitives`, which I left out to keep the change small.
- The marker is plain data, so typing the literal map `{:type :host-fn :name '+}` prints the same text. The existing `{:type :closure ...}` form works the same way.
